# Who must approve a change before it merges (docs/pull-request-gates.md).
#
# The rule: product work merges on its own when every check is green and
# the AI review has no blocking finding. The foundation needs a person:
# sign-in, sessions, permissions, the foundation schema and the backend
# wiring, the app frame, the entitlement decision, the shared services, the
# build and the gates, legal text and the rulebooks. The repository's lead
# approves those. A path with no owner here is product work.
#
# GitHub applies the LAST matching line, and a line with no owner removes
# the owner an earlier line gave: that is how a product releases its own
# paths under an owned directory (see the amplify/ block). The
# `tier-1 review` check reads this file the same way, from the base
# branch as GitHub does, so the check and the PR comment name the same
# files GitHub holds for review and a PR cannot release itself. Keep
# patterns gitignore-shaped: a leading `/` anchors to the repo root, a
# trailing `/` means a directory, `*` never crosses a `/`.
#
# A product mirror keeps this file and adds to it: one line per module to
# release its schema file and its Lambdas (`/amplify/data/modules/<id>.ts`
# is released by the directory line below; `/amplify/functions/<id>-*/`
# with no owner releases the Lambdas), and an owner line for a module
# whose data is regulated (so its whole tree needs a person).

