# The backend: the foundation schema, auth, entitlements, record access,
# the data domains, the shared services (Assist, export, media, notify),
# the foundation Lambdas and the CDK wiring. Everything under amplify/ is
# held unless a line below releases it. A module's own schema file is
# module work: its tables, on its own data domain, behind the entitlement
# gate the foundation applies to every module table. The gates still hold
# one that adds a public, guest or authenticated rule (scripts/pr-gates),
# and the AI review holds one whose content is Tier 1.
/amplify/                              @bax1billion
/amplify/data/modules/

# The seam registries, where a module adds its own line (its tables and
# commands in vertical.ts, its data domain, an export provider, an Assist
# helper). Released: the `tier-1 review` check reads them line by line
# instead (scripts/pr-gates/rules.mjs `additiveRegistryChange`,
# docs/pull-request-gates.md § 2 "Registry lines"). A file that only gained
# the PR's own module lines is module work; any other edit to one of them
# is Tier 1 by that check. GitHub cannot hold a file by what changed in it,
# so the hold lives in the check. A product with the composition test
# (vertical.test.ts) and the audit log policy adds their lines here.
/amplify/data/vertical.ts
/amplify/data/domains/assignments.ts
/amplify/data/domains/registry.ts
